;; The programs of the AOT level whose timeout is their speed (bin/oi check --aot; doc/ocaml/OCAML-SURVEY.md, "As built: review 008's fixes", finding 2
;; and 7): a program listed here that is stopped by the level's CPU limit (OI_TIMEOUT seconds of CPU, bin/lib/limit.bash) is the result "slow",
;; which test/ocaml/divergences-aot.edn's and divergences-suite-aot.edn's speed class matches; a timeout of a program not listed is a failure, and a
;; listed program that passes is reported stale. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 "basic/tailcalls"
 ;; gate 13c (2026-11-14; the user, 2026-11-14, round 38): each run alone on stage 0 with the night's dumps, GOMAXPROCS=1, GOMEMLIMIT
 ;; 900MiB, two at once on a quiet host, against the level's 140 s of CPU (OI_TIMEOUT 120 + O2J_LOAD_ALLOWANCE 20): md5 159.4 s (passes,
 ;; also 159.6 s with jdk/ocaml before OC216), hamming 152.2 s (passes), lists_in_minor 192.3 s (exit 2, its known Memprof result);
 ;; oi runs them in 1.4, 3.1 and 3.2 s. Their timeout is their speed at the light level
 "statmemprof/lists_in_minor"
 ;; queue 438 (OC218's heap model at the light level, 2026-11-19): every simulated minor collection with tracked values and every asked one is a
 ;; System/gc over the light level's whole heap (the library's forms, about 700 MB live), and arrays_in_minor's callbacks ask for a minor
 ;; collection every 100 samples: alone, its two check_counts_full_major phases passed (OCaml's counts) in about 11 minutes of CPU, then
 ;; check_no_nested (every word sampled) ran on; minor_heap_edge (its callbacks' 5 million loop turns, 120 s at oi) printed nothing in 600 s.
 ;; Both pass at oi with the same model
 "statmemprof/arrays_in_minor"
 "statmemprof/minor_heap_edge"
 ;; rec-ocaml (2026-11-16): the native path's whole record on a loaded host, 146.6 s of CPU against 140 (alone it passed): the native typer translates as
 ;; ocamlc does (translcore.ae's transl-function: Translcore tuples a function's tuple parameter only under native_code), so each of
 ;; tak's calls allocates its (x, y, z); the oracle path's ocamlopt-flavoured Lambda did not, and passed. oi runs it as ocamlc's
 "misc/taku"
 "lazy/lazy3"
 "lazy/lazy5"
 "lazy/lazy7"
 "lib-buffer/test"
 "lib-bytes-utf/test"
 "lib-dynarray/test"
 "lib-floatarray/floatarray"
 "lib-hashtbl/htbl"
 "lib-marshal/intern_final"
 "lib-random/chi2"
 "match-exception/streams"
 "memory-model/forbidden"
 "memory-model/publish"
 "misc/sorts"
 "opam/uutf/test_uutf"
 "memory-model/forbidden"
 "memory-model/publish"
 "parallel/churn"
 "parallel/major_gc_wait_backup"
 "parallel/tak"
 "weak-ephe-final/weak_array_par"
 "ast-invariants/test"
 "parsetree/test"
 "parallel/fib_threads"
 "lib-filename/quotecommand"
 ;; queue 370: 100 rounds of half the minor heap's words in refs (13 million allocations) at the light level
 "backtrace/backtraces_and_finalizers"
 ;; queue 397 (the VM, arm64 stage 0, each run alone as o2j_run runs it, GOMAXPROCS=1, two interleaved rounds): pr7798's 5 million allocations
 ;; print 0 (it passes, OI_TIMEOUT=900) in 97.5 and 100.2 s of CPU at 355's tip (c8468871a, before queue 370) and 120.5 and 120.4 s at n-all4
 ;; (88b8e7f1a), against the level's 140: since 370 the library's -g (its slots and events' code) holds about 34 MB more of live heap under
 ;; O2J_GOMEMLIMIT's 900 MiB (pr1271's run: 691 to 725 MB, 40 to 47 collections, the collector 39 to 44% of the time), 6.6 s more to load
 ;; and the rest in the collector's more frequent cycles (under 1500 MiB: 63.0 s at 355's tip, 67.1 s at n-all4). Its timeout is its speed. intern finishes with its known Memprof result (status 2,
 ;; aot-known.edn) once it has the CPU: 589 s of wall alone at load 30 on the VM, within 140 s of CPU on the host (round 54); below that its
 ;; timeout is its speed too. lists_in_minor: since queue 331 Gc.Memprof samples and its callbacks run, so its seven checks all run (before,
 ;; the first check's assertion ended it, 192.3 s above): its first check alone takes 188 to 196 s of CPU at 355's tip and 249 to 257 s at
 ;; n-all4 on the VM, the seven past 900 s at either: 331's cause, 370's -g about 30% beside it (presumably pr7798's collector cost; not measured)
 "regression/pr7798/pr7798"
 "statmemprof/intern"
 ;; queue 414 (the VM, arm64 stage 0): o2j's and the light runtime's hot paths and O2J_GOMEMLIMIT's 1500 MiB (DECISION 397-1 (a)) take
 ;; md5, mc_pr586_par, mc_pr586_par2, testmap, testset, fft, bdd, hamming, stable_matching_test, pingpong, finaliser_handover and weaklifetime2
 ;; within the level's limit, and the suite's input_all (recorded by `check --aot --record --only-list`, `suite check ...`); mctest is :light-depth (aot-known.edn). tak stays: 132 s of CPU
 ;; alone, past the limit in the record's batch (load); the hot paths alone (900 MiB): hamming 102 to 82 s, md5 126 to 111 s
 ;; queue 413: the C API at the light level; each of its 41,000 calls copies a 131,072-element bigarray across the boundary (oi too
 ;; is past its limit: eval's :speed, OC65)
 "lib-bigarray/subarraystub"
]
